    "result_text": "All 3 tests pass. The change is complete.\n\n## Summary\n\nThe change request \u2014 *\"Every client needs an email. Do not let me save one without a proper email address.\"* \u2014 was implemented as an additive, full-stack change across all three layers. (The `email` column already existed, so this adds **validation**.)\n\n**Front-end** (`features/clients/`)\n- `queries.ts` \u2014 added a shared `isValidEmail()` helper with an `EMAIL_PATTERN` (one `@`, non-empty local/domain parts, dotted domain).\n- `ClientForm.tsx` \u2014 blocks submit on a blank/malformed email and renders `<p data-testid=\"client-form-email-error\">`. Also surfaces the error if the server rejects (`onError`), and clears it as the user edits. Uncommitted input stays in `useState` per CLAUDE.md rule 4; the write is still a mutation that invalidates `['clients']`.\n\n**Server** (`ClientsPost.java`)\n- Mirrors the same regex and throws `HttpException(HttpStatus.BAD_REQUEST)` for a null/empty/malformed email, so a bad address is rejected before persisting (defence in depth \u2014 the endpoint YAML and logic-class wiring stay one-file-per-endpoint).\n\n**Database** (`db/migration/V2__clients_email_format.sql`)\n- New Flyway migration adding a `clients_email_format` CHECK constraint (`REGEXP_LIKE`) as the last line of defence. V1 was left untouched.\n\nI matched the exact test anchors (`client-form-name`, `client-form-email`, `client-form-submit`, `client-form-email-error`, `client-row-*`) and did not touch any pinned scaffolding or the spec. `bin/e2e` reports **3 passed** (blank rejected, malformed rejected, valid accepted).",
